<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/06461021-a6c2-4175-9651-23653c2b9116> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:description "Soil surface materials are collected in the most representative geomorphic setting for a site.  In general, it useful to include information such as a sample id, name for the sample, collection depth, latitude and longitude, date of collection and soil moisture content/conditions of collection. Information about the landform, land use and vegetation cover are also useful." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Friske, P. W. B., et al. North American soil geochemical landscapes project: Canadian field protocols for collecting mineral soils and measuring soil gas radon and natural radioactivity. Geological Survey of Canada, Open File 6282 (2010): 177.",
        "Simons, B., Wilson, P., Ritchie, A. and Cox, S., 2013, April. ANZSoilML: an Australian-New Zealand standard for exchange of soil data. In EGU General Assembly Conference Abstracts (pp. EGU2013-6802).",
        "http://vocabs.lter-europe.net/EnvThes/30211" ;
    skos:altLabel "soil sample material",
        "soil surface material" ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/98e8d72d-f361-41ed-af9d-6e7f90c1dfce> ;
    skos:definition "A quantity of soil where observations and measurements are performed.",
        "The soil surface is the uppermost boundary of the Earth's crust where the atmosphere, biosphere, and lithosphere meet." ;
    skos:example "1. The bulk density of a soil surface material; 2. 1000 grams of soil are collected." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "soil-surface" ;
    skos:prefLabel "soil surface" ;
    schema:citation "Friske, P. W. B., et al. North American soil geochemical landscapes project: Canadian field protocols for collecting mineral soils and measuring soil gas radon and natural radioactivity. Geological Survey of Canada, Open File 6282 (2010): 177.",
        "Simons, B., Wilson, P., Ritchie, A. and Cox, S., 2013, April. ANZSoilML: an Australian-New Zealand standard for exchange of soil data. In EGU General Assembly Conference Abstracts (pp. EGU2013-6802)." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/07a75262-f9b7-458d-87ee-28614f535da6> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-12-17T03:50:10"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "In vascular plants, branches arise from an axillary bud meristem and from divisions of the meristematic apical cell in non-vascular plants." ;
    dcterms:modified "2022-07-15T03:23:16"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    skos:definition "A shoot axis that develops from an axillary bud meristem or from equal divisions of a meristematic apical cell." ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0025073> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "individual-branch" ;
    skos:prefLabel "plant branch individual"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/08fa4ec4-29ce-4a0f-b7ce-60adcbdb0ebc> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-01-03T03:03:09"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "An outlook zone is a designated zone/area used for ecological surveys and is represented along a particular compass direction (NE, SW, etc.). Observations within the zone are made from a vantage point." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "McCallum K, Bignall J, Cox B, O’Neill S, Sparrow B (2023) Fauna Ground Counts Module. In ‘Ecological Field Monitoring Protocols Manual using the Ecological Monitoring System Australia’. (Eds S O’Neill, K Irvine, A Tokmakoff, B Sparrow). TERN, Adelaide." ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5bf7ae21-a454-440b-bdd7-f2fe982d8de4> ;
    skos:definition "An area/designated zone intended for ecological observations, especially fauna surveys/ground counts."@en ;
    skos:example "A surveyor recording the presence of a target fauna species within an intended 'outlook zone' from a vantage point." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "outlook zone"@en ;
    schema:citation "McCallum K, Bignall J, Cox B, O’Neill S, Sparrow B (2023) Fauna Ground Counts Module. In ‘Ecological Field Monitoring Protocols Manual using the Ecological Monitoring System Australia’. (Eds S O’Neill, K Irvine, A Tokmakoff, B Sparrow). TERN, Adelaide." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/0c30e871-63ae-4f84-a37c-ef6e7ce02928> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-08-05T04:01:37"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A bird occurrence is a sample of a bird or group of birds at a particular point in time. Unlike bird individuals, this may not specifically relate to a distinct physical entity (e.g. a specific bird individual), but provides a sample which may come from an individuals or a group." ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-10-01T06:21:31"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5cd1dbb0-c30e-4c8e-ae1b-0b388638163c> ;
    skos:definition "An existence of bird sampled at a particular place at a particular time." ;
    skos:example "1. A male cassowary with chicks in the Daintree in 2020. 2. A group of migratory birds observed in a wetland region." ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated the heirarchy of the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "bird-occurrence" ;
    skos:prefLabel "bird occurrence"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/0e354d29-e23f-4ba7-84d6-9b58ca289782> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:description "All dead woody materials present in the stand." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Rondeux, J., Sanchez, C. Review of indicators and field methods for monitoring biodiversity within national forest inventories. Core variable: Deadwood. Environ Monit Assess 164, 617–630 (2010). https://doi.org/10.1007/s10661-009-0917-6" ;
    skos:altLabel "dead woody material in a stand" ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/a8b1a7fb-b479-48ff-b706-b3cc4691710b> ;
    skos:definition "The collection of all non-living woody detritus comprising stems, twigs and roots but excluding deadwood parts of living trees in a specific sampled space."@en ;
    skos:example "The abundance of coarse woody debris in a forest." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "stand-dead-wood" ;
    skos:prefLabel "stand dead wood"@en ;
    schema:citation "Rondeux, J., Sanchez, C. Review of indicators and field methods for monitoring biodiversity within national forest inventories. Core variable: Deadwood. Environ Monit Assess 164, 617–630 (2010). https://doi.org/10.1007/s10661-009-0917-6" .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/13dec53e-1062-4060-9281-f133c8269afb> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-04-22T01:45:48"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    skos:definition "A point in space where observations are made or measurements taken." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "spatial point" ;
    skos:topConceptOf <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/19a72ff8-8ab2-41b8-849a-4f9c6af4ac2b> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-16T22:49:57"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A mammal population may refer to one or several individuals of a species sampled from a region." ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-16T23:34:17"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5c93aeef-c625-4117-85be-3a886416f2be> ;
    skos:definition "Group of individuals of a species of mammal (of Class Mammalia) sampled at a particular place at a particular time." ;
    skos:example "1. The total number of Wombats in Cradle mountain, Tasmania.; 2. The count of male indivduals of two species of Gliders (e.g., Acrobates frontalis and Acrobates pygmaeus) in a Eucalypt woodland." ;
    skos:historyNote "Added to the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "mammal population"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/1c8b7ef9-640c-44b7-b3be-bd2ff92c1edd> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-06-26T10:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-06-26T10:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/afc81cca-9122-4e36-823d-31dd765e9257> ;
    skos:definition "The geologic substrate composed of unconsolidated mineral or organic material (e.g. mud, sand, peat) forming the surface of a coastal wetland, on which surface elevation and accretion measurements are taken." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "sediment" ;
    skos:prefLabel "sediment"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/1d21f4a5-996b-405a-a6f6-2e6fff1035fe> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-05-17T03:40:34"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2022-08-26T05:29:24"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.nrs.fs.fed.us/fia/topics/dwm/glossary/> ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    skos:altLabel "downed woody material" ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/a8b1a7fb-b479-48ff-b706-b3cc4691710b> ;
    skos:definition "Woody pieces of trees and shrubs that have been uprooted (no longer supporting growth) or severed from their root system, not self-supporting, and are lying on the ground."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "downed dead wood"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/1f93a3e8-4c78-4b08-85a4-6869c9ee17ac> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:description "A vegetation stand is a sample of a plant community (see Mueller-Dombois & Ellenberg 1974; Allen & Hoekstra 1992). Usually vegetation stands are selected on the basis of uniformity and discreteness (Van Der Maarel and Franklin, 2013). The vegetation included in the stand looks uniform and should be discernible from surrounding vegetation (Van Der Maarel and Franklin, 2013)." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Allen, Timothy FH, and Thomas W. Hoekstra. The confusion between scale‐defined levels and conventional levels of organization in ecology. Journal of vegetation science 1.1 (1990): 5-12.",
        "Ellenberg, Dieter, and Dieter Mueller-Dombois. Aims and methods of vegetation ecology. New York: Wiley, 1974.",
        "Van Der Maarel, Eddy, and Janet Franklin. Vegetation ecology: historical notes and outline. Vegetation ecology 2 (2013): 1-27." ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/2be2d5ce-ca9d-4dff-8e79-948983944f95> ;
    skos:definition "Continuos community of plants occupying a specific area and sufficiently uniform in species composition, structure, age, size, class, distribution." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "vegetation-stand" ;
    skos:prefLabel "vegetation stand" ;
    schema:citation "Allen, Timothy FH, and Thomas W. Hoekstra. The confusion between scale‐defined levels and conventional levels of organization in ecology. Journal of vegetation science 1.1 (1990): 5-12.",
        "Ellenberg, Dieter, and Dieter Mueller-Dombois. Aims and methods of vegetation ecology. New York: Wiley, 1974.",
        "Van Der Maarel, Eddy, and Janet Franklin. Vegetation ecology: historical notes and outline. Vegetation ecology 2 (2013): 1-27." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/2090cfd9-8b6b-497b-9512-497456a18b99> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-11-19T00:47:12"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "In ecology, a habitat is where a species lives or exists. It is where it will derive its food, shelter, and mate for reproduction." ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-17T06:39:04"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000739> ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/4381b1b0-d432-4764-aec3-a26d2b8d85af> ;
    skos:definition "An environmental system which can sustain and allow the growth of an ecological population." ;
    skos:example "1. A tussock grassland is a habitat typified by perennial grasses with a tufted growth habit; 2. A hollow on a eucalypt tree is a habitat where gliders live." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:note "A habitat's specificity to an ecological population differentiates it from other environment classes." ;
    skos:prefLabel "habitat"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/226a127b-7248-476a-84ad-0412a5e3af52> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-08-05T04:32:59"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A single individual from the Mammalia class, which is a physiological independent individual that has some kind of autonomous agency and has a life cycle that allow them to form some kind of reproductive lineages." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Wilson, Robert A., and Matthew Barker. The biological notion of individual. (2007)." ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/1554c27a-e777-49da-abc3-10296734f80b> ;
    skos:definition "A mammal which is physiologically distinct and independent." ;
    skos:example "A possum individual tagged and observed for their feeding behaviour over time." ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated the heirarchy of the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "mammal-individual" ;
    skos:prefLabel "mammal individual"@en ;
    schema:citation "Wilson, Robert A., and Matthew Barker. The biological notion of individual. (2007)." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/2361dea8-598c-4b6f-a641-2b98ff199e9e> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-12-07T06:06:14"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "An animal occurrence is a sample of an animal or group of animals at a particular point and time. Unlike animal individuals, an animal occurrence may not specifically relate to a distinct physical entity (e.g. a specific animal individual), but provides a sample which may come from an individuals or a group." ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-10-15T13:06:49"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/f6a6cdf8-d8cf-4e2d-b2c1-febd8a41a07b> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence> ;
    skos:definition "An existence of an animal or group of animals sampled at a particular place at a particular time." ;
    skos:example "1. A cassowary in the Daintree rainforest in 2020; 2. A pack of dingoes in K'gari (formerly Fraser Island) seen on the 18 of December of 2017." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "animal-occurrence" ;
    skos:prefLabel "animal occurrence"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/2676d764-fe96-4799-ad2d-6706107cdf9e> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-18T01:27:38"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-10-03T04:06:44"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C14340"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/ea6c4b26-2fa1-4d0e-9413-b53f248f2269> ;
    skos:definition "An individual non-vascular plant. Plant that does not have vascular tubes/tissues to transport food and water. It belongs to the division Bryophyta, which includes liverwort, and moss." ;
    skos:example "An individual moss, tagged and identified to a taxonomic rank sampled from a tropical montane rainforest." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "non-vascular plant individual"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/275458c3-2ebf-48d5-bb5a-8b9f9d970a79> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-16T23:38:15"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A population of reptiles is a collection of individuals belonging to the same reptile species, living in the same area." ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-16T23:43:33"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5c93aeef-c625-4117-85be-3a886416f2be> ;
    skos:definition "Group of individuals of the same repte species (Class: Reptilia) living in a given area at a given time." ;
    skos:example "The total count of Squamata (lizards and snakes) in a Protected Area." ;
    skos:historyNote "Added to the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "reptile population"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/2787089d-4f7f-4d08-b59a-cb790b825b54> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-18T03:34:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "Woody plants are perennials that produce secondary growth in the form of wood." ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-18T03:43:49"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/2217ab3c-0359-42a3-9361-b3b895121841> ;
    skos:definition "Woody plants such as trees, palms, shrubs, that are occurring at a specific area at a specific time." ;
    skos:example "An individual or a group of palms sampled from a sub-tropical rainforest site." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "woody vascular plant occurrence"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/2cf3ed29-440e-4a50-9bbc-5aab30df9fcd> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-02-25T01:34:44"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "The whole land surface is viewed as a mosaic of tiles of odd shapes and two sizes. The larger size is composed of mosaics of the smaller ones. Larger tiles (> 600 m across) are called landform patterns. Smaller tiles (~40m across) are called landform elements." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "McDonald, R.C., Isbell, R.F., Speight, J.G., Walker, J. and Hopkins, M.S., 1998. Australian soil and land survey: field handbook (No. Ed. 2). CSIRO publishing." ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/8282fb22-4135-415c-8ca2-317860d102fb> ;
    skos:definition "Visible features of an area of land, including the physical elements of it soils, landforms (LandSurface Feature) , geology (GeologicFeature), water bodies (StreamChannel Feature), living elements of land cover (VegetationFeature), human elements (LandUse Feature) and transitory elements (Climate Feature)." ;
    skos:example "Land surface features such as mountains and hills. Stream channel features such as rivers, lakes and ponds. Land use features including different forms of land use, buildings and structures. Climate feature such as lighting and weather conditions." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "landform" ;
    skos:prefLabel "landform"@en ;
    schema:citation "McDonald, R.C., Isbell, R.F., Speight, J.G., Walker, J. and Hopkins, M.S., 1998. Australian soil and land survey: field handbook (No. Ed. 2). CSIRO publishing." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/338c05d6-cc0e-4a41-ba9c-c5060c4d4501> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-18T01:12:46"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "Woody plants are trees, shrubs and Palms whose shoots are durable and survive over a period of years." ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-10-03T04:33:46"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "https://www.britannica.com/plant/woody-plant"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/b64cfbb3-86a2-43b3-a749-11243805cb85> ;
    skos:definition "These plants are perennials that produce secondary growth in the form of wood." ;
    skos:example "A community of trees and palms sampled from a sub-tropical rainforest site for its total biomass." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "woody vascular plants community"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/415be87e-66e1-4a53-a5c8-3d34ab93036c> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-08-22T05:06:31"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "An individual or a group of Amphibia class observed at a particular geographic location. Amphibians are cold-blooded, smooth-skinned vertebrate which characteristically hatches as an aquatic larva, breathing by gills. When mature, the amphibian breathes with lungs." ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-10-01T06:21:07"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T011"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5cd1dbb0-c30e-4c8e-ae1b-0b388638163c> ;
    skos:definition "An existence of an amphibian sampled at a particular place at a particular time." ;
    skos:example "An individual or a group of frogs of a particular taxonomic rank sampled during a vertebrate fauna survey." ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated the heirarchy of the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "amphibian-occurrence" ;
    skos:prefLabel "amphibian occurrence"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/42f2b20b-89bb-4d65-99de-38282fb860d9> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-18T01:28:54"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "Any individual non-woody vascular plant, i.e., belonging to a herb, grass, forb or fern species for example. They do not produce wood, but have vascular tissues consisting of xylem, which carries water and nutrients from the roots up the stem to the leaves, and the phloem, which carries sugar produced in the leaves to other parts of the plant." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Petruzzello, M. (2024, March 21). herbaceous plant. Encyclopedia Britannica. https://www.britannica.com/plant/herbaceous-plant" ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/57c778e4-5a82-4dfd-8087-d616ac629ab1> ;
    skos:definition "A non-woody vascular plant individual is an individual that does not produce secondary growth in the form of wood." ;
    skos:example "An individual fern, tagged and identified to its species level and studied for its growth over multiple site visits." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "non-woody vascular plant individual"@en ;
    schema:citation "Petruzzello, M. (2024, March 21). herbaceous plant. Encyclopedia Britannica. https://www.britannica.com/plant/herbaceous-plant" .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/4362c8f2-b3cc-4816-b5a2-fb7bb4c0cff5> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-05-06T05:14:19"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T22:42:42"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5bf7ae21-a454-440b-bdd7-f2fe982d8de4> ;
    skos:definition "A transportable frame (usually a square made out of PVC tube, metal rod or wood) used to isolate a standard unit of area for study of the distribution of item(s) over a large area (e.g. a plot)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "quadrat"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/4507e510-bf25-467b-a97e-abd56776507a> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2023-12-12T03:57:59"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "Animal evidence provides information about the signs or the presence of an animal at a given location and time."@en ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-10-01T06:15:48"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECO_0000000"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    skos:altLabel "fauna evidence" ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/f6a6cdf8-d8cf-4e2d-b2c1-febd8a41a07b> ;
    skos:definition "Any information/knowledge that is used to support an assertion of the presence of an animal in a geographic area."@en ;
    skos:example "1. The footprints/tracks of dingoes are used as signs-based evidence to support the presence of dingos in Fraser Island; 2. The presence of reptile detected by skin sheds after ecdysis in a survey area."@en ;
    skos:historyNote "Added as a concept under for the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "animal-evidence" ;
    skos:prefLabel "animal evidence"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/45a73139-f6bf-47b7-88d4-4b2865755545> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-12-16T04:48:41"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A fungi occurrence is a sample of a fungi at a particular point and time." ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-17T06:37:41"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/1a017998-f59d-43f8-ac47-bea75e50d24d> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://rs.tdwg.org/dwc/terms/Occurrence> ;
    skos:definition "An existence of a fungi sampled at a particular place at a particular time." ;
    skos:example "1.The presence of mycorrhizae in soils. 2. The presence of basidiomycetes on a log of wood." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "fungi-occurrence" ;
    skos:prefLabel "fungi occurrence"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/47fbe947-4f8b-4586-9cf7-13a610f8aedb> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-08-22T06:11:43"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A single individual from the Amphibia class. Amphibians are cold-blooded, smooth-skinned vertebrate which characteristically hatches as an aquatic larva, breathing by gills. When mature, the amphibian breathes with lungs." ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-10-01T06:19:59"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T011"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/1554c27a-e777-49da-abc3-10296734f80b> ;
    skos:definition "An amphibian which is a physiologically distinct and independent." ;
    skos:example "An individual frog or toad in a given geographic location that has been identified and observations/measurements made on their acoustic behaviour over time." ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated the heirarchy of the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "amphibian-individual" ;
    skos:prefLabel "amphibian individual"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/481a315d-e963-4f93-88e5-027b5369c72d> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-18T03:48:49"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "Non-woody plants are those that do not produce secondary growth in the form of wood. They include herbaceous species such as grasses, forbs, ferns, etc." ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-18T04:51:37"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/95e72362-8575-46e9-bc60-a45f48b95390> ;
    skos:definition "The total number of individuals of non-woody vascular plants sampled at a specific location and time." ;
    skos:example "A study on the population size of all the Cyperus spp. (sedges) from a conservation area following a cyclone event." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "non-woody vascular plant population"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/51e0e6c3-b833-4f32-8d0e-00cc76031b83> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:description "A fish occurrence is a sample of a fish (aquatic, gill-bearing animals) at a particular point and time. A fish occurrence may come from an individual or a group." ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-16T23:29:06"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5cd1dbb0-c30e-4c8e-ae1b-0b388638163c> ;
    skos:definition "An existence of fish sampled at a particular place at a particular time." ;
    skos:example "A collection of mangrove snappers sampled in Burdekin river." ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated the heirarchy of the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "fish-occurrence" ;
    skos:prefLabel "fish occurrence"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5916bd8d-ba9f-45d1-b761-20d186f23311> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-16T23:32:35"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "An amphibian population may refer to one or several individuals of an amphibian species sampled from a given region." ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-16T23:37:49"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5c93aeef-c625-4117-85be-3a886416f2be> ;
    skos:definition "Group of individuals of a species of amphibians (of Class Amphibia) sampled at a particular place at a particular time." ;
    skos:example "The total number of male cane toads sampled along an elevation transect in north Queensland." ;
    skos:historyNote "Added to the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "amphibian population"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5ba6ba64-cf48-4c1e-93e5-3892c2b92f4b> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-08-22T00:28:37"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "An fish indvidual is a physiological independent individual that has some kind of autonomous agency and has a life cycle that allow them to form some kind of reproductive lineages." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Wilson, Robert A., and Matthew Barker. The biological notion of individual. (2007)." ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/1554c27a-e777-49da-abc3-10296734f80b> ;
    skos:definition "A physiologically distinct and independent organism (i.e., aquatic, gill-bearing animal)." ;
    skos:example "An individual fish in a stream tagged for studying their feeding activity over time. " ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated the heirarchy of the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "fish-individual" ;
    skos:prefLabel "fish individual"@en ;
    schema:citation "Wilson, Robert A., and Matthew Barker. The biological notion of individual. (2007)." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5ca63df3-55b2-4bf0-9720-e7f7130bb64c> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-18T01:13:05"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "The non-woody vascular plants (also known as herbaceous plants) are grasses, sedges, herbs, ferns, and forbs. " ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Petruzzello, M. (2024, March 21). herbaceous plant. Encyclopedia Britannica. https://www.britannica.com/plant/herbaceous-plant" ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/b64cfbb3-86a2-43b3-a749-11243805cb85> ;
    skos:definition "These plants do not have a woody stem, but have vascular tissue, consisting of xylem, which carries water and nutrients from the roots up the stem to the leaves, and the phloem, which carries sugar produced in the leaves to other parts of the plant." ;
    skos:example "A community of grasses and sedges sampled from an arid location." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "non-woody vascular plants community"@en ;
    schema:citation "Petruzzello, M. (2024, March 21). herbaceous plant. Encyclopedia Britannica. https://www.britannica.com/plant/herbaceous-plant" .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/60d7edf8-98c6-43e9-841c-e176c334d270> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:description "In ecology, plant individuals are often studied as part of a plant community, which is a group of plant species living and interacting with one another in a specific location. Plant individuals are important components of ecological systems because they are primary producers, meaning that they are able to convert sunlight into energy through photosynthesis, and provide food and habitat for other organisms." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Cook, Robert Edward. Asexual reproduction: a further consideration. The American Naturalist 113.5 (1979): 769-772.",
        "Harper, J. L. Modules, branches, and the capture of resources. In Population biology and evolution of clonal organisms.(Eds JBC Jackson, LW Buss, RE Cook) pp. 1–33. (1985)." ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5914> ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/881bcb98-1c31-4710-a9a4-58dbe1bc4a95> ;
    skos:definition "In ecological terms, a plant individual is a single, physically distinct organism belonging to the plant kingdom. This can refer to a single plant, such as a tree or shrub, or a single member of a plant species, such as a single blade of grass or a single leaf." ;
    skos:example "In the TERN vocab collection 'plant individual' is specifically used as a feature of interest representing an individual plant (i.e., either a tree, shrub or palm) in a given geographic location, and is tagged with a unique identification label with repeated observations/measurements such as plant height, stem diameter, etc. perfomed on that individual over time." ;
    skos:historyNote "Added as a narrower concept of 'plant' in the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "plant-individual" ;
    skos:prefLabel "plant individual" ;
    schema:citation "Cook, Robert Edward. Asexual reproduction: a further consideration. The American Naturalist 113.5 (1979): 769-772.",
        "Harper, J. L. Modules, branches, and the capture of resources. In Population biology and evolution of clonal organisms.(Eds JBC Jackson, LW Buss, RE Cook) pp. 1–33. (1985)." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/61311a0e-5b09-406c-9f64-b0637271ecf2> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-04-20T04:49:27"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T22:46:24"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/8cadf069-01d7-4420-b454-cae37740c2a2> ;
    skos:definition "A smaller sampling unit established within a larger plot, used to collect more detailed or specific measurements of abiotic or biotic properties. Subplots help capture variability within the main plot and support finer-scale analysis.",
        "The plot that is part of the main survey plot." ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated on 10/09/2025: added this concept to Site type scheme, updated the definition so that it fits in both Attribute and Site Type scheme." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d>,
        <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/dd085299-ae86-4371-ae15-61dfa432f924> ;
    skos:prefLabel "subplot"@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/dd085299-ae86-4371-ae15-61dfa432f924> .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/62a51999-f3ca-41d2-8576-3a053dd116a6> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-08-05T03:58:45"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A population of birds (vertebrates class Aves) is a collection of individuals belonging to the same bird species, living in the same area." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Begon, Michael, Martin Mortimer, and David J. Thompson. Population ecology: a unified study of animals and plants. John Wiley & Sons, 2009." ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5c93aeef-c625-4117-85be-3a886416f2be> ;
    skos:definition "Group of individuals of the same bird species (class Aves) living within a given area." ;
    skos:example "A flock of Galah feeding on fruits." ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated the heirarchy of the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "bird-population" ;
    skos:prefLabel "bird population"@en ;
    schema:citation "Begon, Michael, Martin Mortimer, and David J. Thompson. Population ecology: a unified study of animals and plants. John Wiley & Sons, 2009." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/62de2d02-4635-4835-b005-83890d755c34> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-18T03:17:17"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-10-03T04:06:57"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C14340"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/ea6c4b26-2fa1-4d0e-9413-b53f248f2269> ;
    skos:definition "Non-vascular plants that are occurring at a specific region at a specific time. They are plants that do not have vascular tubes/tissues to transport food and water. It belongs to the division Bryophyta, which includes liverwort, and moss." ;
    skos:example "An individual or a group of lichens sampled from a rocky area." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "non-vascular plant occurrence"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/63e83f29-7240-499b-a6ca-015b265beda7> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-04-22T01:45:43"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    skos:definition "Straight line through space along which observations are made or measurements taken." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "transect" ;
    skos:topConceptOf <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/6631aee8-6b8c-4ce0-ae0b-27ad55263a7e> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-04-16T05:23:50"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-04-19T04:45:14"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/c242f606-1df2-4222-a5f1-a899ae66fde4> ;
    skos:definition "A vertebrate community (i.e., animals that possess or develop a vertebral column) are a group/s or vertebrates of different species and or populations living in a geographic area." ;
    skos:example "A collection of vertebrates (such as birds and mammals) from a wetland region." ;
    skos:historyNote "Added to the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "vertebrate community"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/699b7fcb-6816-4f2a-9f2f-72b8a913f1d0> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-09-19T03:07:43"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "Dead plant material (leaves, bark, needles, and twigs) that have fallen to the ground in a specific sampled space." ;
    dcterms:modified "2023-06-23T05:56:27"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/e6ed6e58-5916-4d31-9ed5-109ab3436fce> ;
    skos:definition "Dead plant material (not wood) that have fallen to the ground in a sampled contiguous community of plants." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "stand-plant-litter" ;
    skos:prefLabel "stand plant litter"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/6ac5044b-ffac-4cfb-b135-1983e0ea2f7a> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-12-06T01:39:41"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "Plant disturbance occurs when a plant is damaged, its growth is restricted, or its reproduction is limited. This can be natural and/or human induced." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Johnson, E. A., & Miyanishi, K. (Eds.). (2010). Plant disturbance ecology: the process and the response. Elsevier." ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/d4fc54b1-0ad3-4512-86b7-d42b121ece45> ;
    skos:definition "Events that disrupts individual plant or plant components directly, impacting its physical structure and functions." ;
    skos:example "Frequency and intensity of fires or pests on individual plants; Anthropogenic disturbance such as logging, lopping, etc." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "plant disturbance"@en ;
    schema:citation "Johnson, E. A., & Miyanishi, K. (Eds.). (2010). Plant disturbance ecology: the process and the response. Elsevier." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/6d40d71e-58cd-4f75-8304-40c01fe5f74c> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-02-25T01:00:37"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "All weather conditions for a given location over a period of time. Climate refers to atmospheric changes over longer periods of time, usually defined as 30 years or more." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "https://education.nationalgeographic.org/resource/weather-or-climate-whats-difference/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/db6d3a22-8bf4-4e27-a9a4-a49e228b6f52> ;
    skos:definition "Climate is commonly defined as the weather averaged, or otherwise summarised, over a period of time much longer than the duration of any phenomenon that constitutes weather." ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001082> ;
    skos:example "A change in climate forecasted for Litchfield, based on historical climate records from the flux tower. Climate based on region types include: equatorial, tropical, sub-tropical, temperate, desert, grassland." ;
    skos:historyNote "Added as a narrower of 'atmosphere' in the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "climate" ;
    skos:prefLabel "climate"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/6e8feb2a-6e55-42d0-9e1e-0d85bed27843> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-08-05T03:56:43"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A bird indvidual is a physiological independent individual that has some kind of autonomous agency and has a life cycle that allow them to form some kind of reproductive lineages." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Wilson, Robert A., and Matthew Barker. The biological notion of individual. (2007)." ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/1554c27a-e777-49da-abc3-10296734f80b> ;
    skos:definition "A physiologically distinct and independent bird individual." ;
    skos:example "An individual bird tagged with a ring band for studying their activity over time." ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated the heirarchy of the TERN Feature Type (Release version, 2024)." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "bird-individual" ;
    skos:prefLabel "bird individual"@en ;
    schema:citation "Wilson, Robert A., and Matthew Barker. The biological notion of individual. (2007)." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/6f3aedf7-4ab8-4ba5-82af-928ec9d51c7f> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2024-01-03T03:02:37"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A vantage point is a view point, usually high and provides a clear scenic aerial perspective/vision of an area."@en ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T22:54:54"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5bf7ae21-a454-440b-bdd7-f2fe982d8de4> ;
    skos:definition "A place, especially a high place, that provides a good, clear view of an area."@en ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch:> <https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/vantage-point> ;
    skos:example "A surveyor studying the presence of a fauna (pest) from a 'vantage point'." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "vantage point"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/6fb57064-7198-4df9-bf7c-86b73f69da66> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-04-09T00:32:52"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T22:47:09"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/5bf7ae21-a454-440b-bdd7-f2fe982d8de4> ;
    skos:definition "A designated area within a larger survey site that is treated as a separate unit for sampling or data collection. Subsites allow researchers to capture spatial variation across different parts of the main site. Subsites can be of type plots, transects, quadrats or simply point locations within the site." ;
    skos:historyNote "Updated on 10/09/2025: activated the deprecated concept, move it from Feature type to Site type scheme, and added definition." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "subsite"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/7fd49a58-6b46-497c-b5d6-68cda55531df> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2025-09-09T02:09:46"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Wood, S., Stephens, H., Foulkes, J., Ebsworth, E. and Bowman, D., (2012). AusPlots Forests Survey Protocols Manual. Version 1.6 page 61-70.Terrestrial Ecosystem Research Network and The University of Adelaide Press." ;
    owl:deprecated true ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/e6ed6e58-5916-4d31-9ed5-109ab3436fce> ;
    skos:definition "Fine litter includes detached leaves of trees or shrubs, twigs ≤ 6 mm diameter and any detached part of grasses or herbs." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "fine litter"@en ;
    schema:citation "Wood, S., Stephens, H., Foulkes, J., Ebsworth, E. and Bowman, D., (2012). AusPlots Forests Survey Protocols Manual. Version 1.6 page 61-70.Terrestrial Ecosystem Research Network and The University of Adelaide Press." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/80c39b95-0912-4267-bb66-2fa081683723> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:description "A soil profile is a vertical section of a soil from the soil surface through all its horizons to parent material, other consolidated substrate material or selected depth in unconsolidated material. Because soil depth varies between very wide limits the depth of examination in practice frequently may not exceed 1.5–2 m." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "McDonald, R.C., Isbell, R.F., Speight, J.G., Walker, J. and Hopkins, M.S., 1998. Australian soil and land survey: field handbook (No. Ed. 2). CSIRO publishing." ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/98e8d72d-f361-41ed-af9d-6e7f90c1dfce> ;
    skos:definition "A collection of vertical sections of soil, usually collected to 1m depth." ;
    skos:example "The depth of the soil profile." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "soil-profile" ;
    skos:prefLabel "soil profile" ;
    schema:citation "McDonald, R.C., Isbell, R.F., Speight, J.G., Walker, J. and Hopkins, M.S., 1998. Australian soil and land survey: field handbook (No. Ed. 2). CSIRO publishing." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/8a68b4a9-167b-40f0-9222-293a2d20ffee> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2021-04-21T06:28:27"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "A population of animals is a collection of individuals belonging to the same species, living in the same area. Vital rates such as survival, growth, migration structure the population size." ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19T05:29:51+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "Begon, Michael, Martin Mortimer, and David J. Thompson. Population ecology: a unified study of animals and plants. John Wiley & Sons, 2009.",
        "Silvertown, Jonathan, and Deborah Charlesworth. Introduction to plant population biology. John Wiley & Sons, 2009." ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://vocabs.lter-europe.net/EnvThes/20715> ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/f6a6cdf8-d8cf-4e2d-b2c1-febd8a41a07b> ;
    skos:definition "The total number of individuals or groups of the same animal species living within a given area." ;
    skos:example "1. A colony of red ants in a study plot in Kakadu National Park, NT; 2. The number of male and female Koalas on a Eucalypt woodland, Fig Tree Pocket, Brisbane." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:notation "animal-population" ;
    skos:prefLabel "animal population"@en ;
    schema:citation "Begon, Michael, Martin Mortimer, and David J. Thompson. Population ecology: a unified study of animals and plants. John Wiley & Sons, 2009.",
        "Silvertown, Jonathan, and Deborah Charlesworth. Introduction to plant population biology. John Wiley & Sons, 2009." .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/8cd716ed-7d4f-4c44-81ba-c921cb431962> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-09-19T23:52:34"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:description "Dead or alive plant organic matter characteristics relevant to its flammability sampled over a transect." ;
    dcterms:modified "2023-06-23T05:47:16"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:source "https://www.ecologyandsociety.org/vol7/iss1/art9/des_fuel_load.html" ;
    skos:broader <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/df7fd606-8145-4206-b66e-b86444888802> ;
    skos:definition "Sample of dead and alive vegetation matter relevant to its flammability using a transect." ;
    skos:example "The fuel load in a transect." ;
    skos:inScheme <http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/68af3d25-c801-4089-afff-cf701e2bd61d> ;
    skos:prefLabel "transect vegetation fuel sample"@en .

<http://linked.data.gov.au/def/tern-cv/972669a7-8a3c-4bd6-9d24-04606fcdd773> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2022-03-10T05:57:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:modified "2023-06-23T06:31:23"^^xsd:dateTime ;
